Subject: [PATCH] usb: support mici PMI8998 VBUS and fault recovery

Add a distinct PMI8998 regulator with the stock 250 mA current encoding,
protected HALT1_IN8 sequence and bounded boost readiness polling. Forward
OTG/VCONN faults through standard regulator and TCPM APIs.

Keep USBIN restore state across failed transitions. Dedicated-rail cleanup
runs the complete provider disable even when CMD_OTG is already off, never
re-enables a failed output, and quiesces callbacks/TCPM before shutdown.
The charger must remain disabled and the connector the sole VBUS consumer.

Register definitions and the source/input sequence follow the existing
commaai/agnos-kernel-sdm845 SMB2 driver. See kernel/USB.md for provenance,
fault tests and the remaining physical acceptance checks.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,usb-vbus-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,usb-vbus-regulator.yaml
